> the square root of x plus 1
  note: what does "the square root of" apply to: read as sqrt(x) + ..., not sqrt(x + ...) (say "the square root of the quantity ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(x) = sqrt(x) + 1
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = sqrt(x) + 1
  -> real
> what is the range of x squared for a byte x?
  note: "byte" without signed or unsigned: read as unsigned, u8, not signed, i8 (say "unsigned byte", or "assume bytes are signed")
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x^2
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u8:
  0..249   (44 distinct values)
  values: 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, 25, 33, 36, 41, 49, 57, 64..65, 68, 73, 81, 89, 97, 100, 105, 113, 121, 129, 132, 137, 144..145, ...
  fits in u8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> the log of x
  note: "log" without a base: read as the natural log, ln, not log base 2 or log base 10 (say "natural log", "log base 2" or "log base 10", or "assume log means base 2")
  ucas: it(x) = log(x)
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = log(x)
  -> real
